                    {
                        "sense_id": "adf5d248-737d-3c1c-b7d0-05f0b0d40e3b",
                        "entry_id": "387b039c-07e5-3033-a5b7-9198f96d0655",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Appended by prescription, that is, a personal usage for a considerable time; said of a thing of inheritance belonging to another inheritance which is superior or more worthy; as, an advowson, common, etc., which may be appendant to a manor, common of fishing to a freehold, a seat in church to a house."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e2a5597-ffe5-48d7-aabf-5a90a536dede",
                                "sense_id": "adf5d248-737d-3c1c-b7d0-05f0b0d40e3b",
                                "text": "If A. be ſeiſed of a mannor whereunto the franchiſe of waife and ſtray and ſuch like are appendant, and the King purchaſeth the mannor with the appurtenances, now are the royall Franchiſes reunited to the Crowne, and not appendant to the Mannor, […]"
                            }
                        ]
